Smart Crane Control System using Industrial Shields ESP32 PLC14

This project is a smart crane control system developed using the Industrial Shields ESP32 PLC14 and a BLE-based mobile application. The system enables wireless crane operation, real-time monitoring, user management, and web-based configuration.

Features
BLE Mobile App Control

The ESP32 PLC14 connects with a BLE mobile application to control crane operations wirelessly. The mobile app provides the following crane controls:

UP motion control
DOWN motion control
LEFT motion control
RIGHT motion control
Emergency Stop (E-STOP)

The BLE connection allows operators to control the crane safely and conveniently from a mobile device.

Integrated Webserver

The PLC14 hosts a built-in webserver for monitoring, configuration, and system management.

Webserver Functions
Real-Time Monitoring

The web dashboard displays:

BLE mobile app connection status
Current crane motion status
UP
DOWN
LEFT
RIGHT
STOP
E-STOP status

This allows operators and administrators to monitor the crane system in real time from any browser connected to the network.

User Management System

The webserver includes a user management section for BLE application authentication.

Features
Add new users
Manage BLE app login credentials
Restrict unauthorized access to crane controls

This improves system security and user access control.

Output Configuration

The system includes an output configuration page accessible through the webserver.

Features
Configure PLC output pin assignments
Change output mappings without modifying firmware
Flexible setup for different crane wiring configurations
Network Settings (Phase 2)

In Phase 2, a new Network Settings section was added to the webserver.

Features
Edit BLE device name
Configure WiFi SSID
Configure WiFi password/credentials
Update network settings directly from the web interface

This allows easy reconfiguration of communication settings without uploading new firmware to the PLC.

Motion Expansion (Phase 3)

In Phase 3, two additional crane motion controls were added:

LEFT motion
RIGHT motion

The mobile app, PLC logic, and webserver monitoring system were updated to support these new motion outputs.

This enables multi-directional crane movement and improves overall crane operation flexibility.

Technologies Used
Industrial Shields ESP32 PLC14
ESP32 BLE
Embedded Webserver
WiFi Communication
Arduino Framework
HTML / CSS / JavaScript
Applications
Industrial crane automation
Wireless crane control systems
Smart hoist systems
Industrial IoT monitoring
Remote machine operation
